  "transcript": "Provider: Hi. All right. My name's <clinician name>. What brings you in?\nPatient: I don't know. Got bit by a dog.\nProvider: Was it my dog?\nPatient: No. He likes to bite.\nProvider: Yeah.\nPatient: So, where's the bite?\nProvider: Bite's here. That's not really Yeah, it's not that's not really what's bothering me. It's, you know, all that.\nPatient: Did you fall?\nProvider: Yeah. They kind of just threw me on the ground and There were two big dogs. Yeah.\nPatient: She's laughing about it.\nProvider: Yeah, I know. She reposted me on social media.\nPatient: Who'd you bring with you?\nProvider: This is my girlfriend.\nPatient: Oh. Okay. So, you were hanging out, doing things, fell, and yeah.\nProvider: Yeah.\nPatient: So, can you bend your knee? Are you able to walk? It's going to hurt.\nProvider: Yeah, that's where I'm at.\nPatient: Oh, I always do this.\nProvider: Yeah, that's That's Can you stand?\nProvider: I mean, I can stand, but like any any movement, like putting pressure on it, it's just Yeah, it's that sucks.\nPatient: We can take a picture.\nProvider: Okay.\nPatient: It's probably not broken.\nProvider: No, I wouldn't say so.\nPatient: Like 90% probably not broken.\nProvider: For sure. I don't think it's broken.\nPatient: Probably 99. It's going to hurt.\nProvider: Yeah.\nPatient: Until it cools down, you're going to have to ice pack it. Um, I actually just did this with my dog.\nProvider: Oh, really?\nPatient: I think maybe it was my dog. Oh my gosh.\nProvider: Um, I was on my bike, though. Oh, jeez. We were cruising pretty fast and He's not fun.\nProvider: Yeah.\nPatient: So, bit you, bit you. Teeth. Okay. Not too bad. Nothing to close. Did you wash it?\nProvider: I haven't had the chance to, no.\nPatient: Okay. So, I'm going to have <clinician name> come in and wash it with soap.\nProvider: And Huh? That's That's cool. Okay.",
